  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Edge",
      "items": [
        "The ALB is the only internet-facing resource: it spans both public subnets and terminates TLS with an ACM certificate under ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06",
        "Port 80 answers 301 to HTTPS; port 443 forwards to the frontend by default and sends /api/* straight to the backend target group",
        "A regional WAF web ACL is attached to the ALB - Core Rule Set, Known Bad Inputs and a rate-based rule of 2000 requests per 5 minutes per IP, all starting in Count"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Egress is inspected",
      "items": [
        "Each private subnet routes 0.0.0.0/0 to the Network Firewall endpoint of its own AZ, and the firewall forwards to the NAT gateway of that AZ",
        "The stateful rule group passes only TLS (443), DNS (53 tcp and udp) and established returns; everything else is dropped",
        "Security groups cap egress at 443 plus DNS and the NACLs repeat that policy, so there is no route around the firewall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One private subnet per service",
      "items": [
        "Each service gets its own private subnet, route table, NACL and security group: 10.0.10.0/24 for the backend in us-east-1a and 10.0.11.0/24 for the frontend in us-east-1b",
        "One reusable module builds each cluster with its own node group (1 x t3.small, ON_DEMAND, AL2023) and a dedicated security group",
        "The events service is a ClusterIP inside the backend cluster, so gRPC never crosses the ALB"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Identity, images and the emulator",
      "items": [
        "One cluster role and one node role per cluster, plus an OIDC provider and one IRSA role per service whose inline policy names only its own table",
        "Three Amazon ECR repositories with IMMUTABLE tags: a published tag is never overwritten and the node role can only pull images",
        "The same Terraform runs against the local Floci emulator with every endpoint on port 4566; EKS addons are declared but disabled because Floci has no CreateAddon"
      ]
    }
  ]
